# Line endings, and why this file has to exist.
#
# The site is served as bytes. Two of those bytes-exact guarantees are load-bearing:
#
#   1. SUBRESOURCE INTEGRITY. index.html/support.js pin the vendored React, ReactDOM and Babel with
#      sha384 `integrity` attributes. If Git rewrites those files' line endings on checkout, their
#      hashes change, the browser BLOCKS them, and the app never boots.
#
#   2. The static legal pages are DERIVED by rendering the real site (tools/build-static-pages.py).
#      A site that cannot boot renders only index.html's static <main> fallback — which is the HOME
#      page — so the generator writes four copies of the front page over the privacy policy, terms,
#      deletion and support pages, and its size guard cannot tell because a wrong page is just as
#      long as a right one.
#
# Both happened. On Windows, `core.autocrlf` defaults to true and there was no .gitattributes, so a
# clone got react.production.min.js at 10,782 bytes where the repository (and the live site) hold
# 10,751 — thirty-one added carriage returns, three failed integrity checks, a dead preview, and a
# generator that quietly produced the wrong legal pages. (2026-08-27)

# Everything is LF, in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except the vendored libraries, which are never touched at all. Their bytes are hashed.
assets/vendor/** -text

# Binary assets, likewise untouched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
